# Line endings are pinned so a fresh clone produces the same bytes everywhere.
#
# core.autocrlf on a Windows machine rewrites the working tree to CRLF while the
# repository stores LF. Nothing in this project needs CRLF: there is no .bat or
# .cmd file, and Windows PowerShell, the C# overlay compiler and gofmt all read
# LF. Pinning the whole tree keeps a clone from silently diverging file by file,
# and keeps a Windows checkout and a CI runner byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored driver and the native overlay are compiled and executed as they
# are, so their bytes must survive a checkout unchanged.
/vendor/**  text eol=lf
/native/**  text eol=lf

# Formats that must never be line-ending converted, even if a heuristic would
# call them text.
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.ico  binary
*.png  binary
*.tgz  binary
